(423, 'AFID Infrastructure Grants, Virginia Dept. of Agriculture and Consumer Services (VDACS)', 'State', 'VA', 'Reimbursable capital projects at new and existing food hubs, farmers markets, commercial kitchens and value-added processing or packaging facilities', 'Startup; Scaling; Mature', 'Up to $50K', '1:1 cash from locality (reduced for economically distressed localities)', 'Closed: spring 2026 round due April 30, 2026; fall 2026 round listed as closed; two rounds per fiscal year, next round expected spring 2027', 'Political subdivisions (counties, cities, towns, IDAs, planning district commissions) apply; hubs partner with their locality. Food hubs named as a priority. Past award: Bath County $50K for a commissary kitchen and food aggregator (Mar 2025). State-funded (created 2021).', 'https://www.vdacs.virginia.gov/press-releases-260317-vdacs-opens-afid-infrastructure-grant-application-spring-2026.shtml', '2026-11-22', false),
