(426, 'Virginia Agriculture Food Assistance Program (VAFAP), VDACS', 'State', 'VA', 'Reimburses charitable food organizations for buying minimally processed Virginia-grown products to distribute to food-insecure residents (functions like a state LFPA)', 'Scaling; Mature', '$15K–150K (spring 2026: 22 grants, $1.1M); $2.0M available fall 2026', 'Not stated', 'Open: fall 2026 window Nov 16, 2026 to Jan 4, 2027, 5 p.m.; twice-yearly rounds', 'Nonprofit or community-based charitable food assistance organizations apply. A nonprofit hub doing charitable distribution may qualify; for-profit hubs benefit as suppliers. Funding source (state or federal) not stated on page.', 'https://www.vdacs.virginia.gov/virginia-agriculture-food-assistance-program.shtml', '2026-11-22', false),
