(428, 'Virginia Food Access Investment Fund (VFAIF), VDACS', 'State', 'VA', 'Construction, rehabilitation, equipment and expansion of grocery stores, small food retailers and innovative food retail in low-income areas', 'Startup; Scaling', 'Standard up to $50K; large-scale retail awards $237.5K–250K (2025)', 'Not stated', 'Closed: pre-proposal window closed; 2025 awards announced Aug 19, 2025 (10 grants, about $1.04M); next round not announced', 'Projects need a retail component, SNAP acceptance and Virginia Fresh Match participation. Hub fit shown: Mid-Atlantic Black Farmers Caucus got $250K (2025) for a food hub with aggregation, packing and freezer storage.', 'https://www.vdacs.virginia.gov/press-releases-250819-virginia-food-access-investment-fund-awards.shtml', '2026-11-22', false),
